<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to July 11.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in year	    Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			  Price     change</p>
<p> 1  Oil Search		   3.70     186.82</p>
<p> 2  Sthn Pac Pete		3.90     100.00</p>
<p> 3  Transurban Group	1115.00	74.35</p>
<p> 4  Natl Aust Bank	    19.95	73.78</p>
<p> 5  Howard Smith		13.40	72.68</p>
<p> 6  A N Z Bank		  10.15	66.94</p>
<p> 7  Southcorp Hldgs	    4.96	63.70</p>
<p> 8  FLC-Building div	   3.96	63.42</p>
<p> 9  Hardie Inds		  4.17	62.89</p>
<p>10  Wesfarmers		  11.95	62.59</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in year	   Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     change</p>
<p> 1  Acacia Resources	   1.39     -52.23</p>
<p> 2  Newcrest Mining	    2.50     -48.45</p>
<p> 3  Sons Of Gwalia	     4.88     -41.56</p>
<p> 4  Goldfields		   1.70     -40.35</p>
<p> 5  Plutonic Rsc		 3.81     -37.34</p>
<p> 6  Great Central		2.26     -35.98</p>
<p> 7  Davids Limited	     1.21     -30.46</p>
<p> 8  RGC			    4.36     -28.64</p>
<p> 9  Centaur Min&amp;Expl	   1.25     -26.04</p>
<p>10  Crown			  2.13     -21.19</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
